---
id: roasted-broccoli
title: Roasted Broccoli
category: modular_cooked_veg

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 400

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Set the #oven to convection 220°C (425°F) and let it preheat fully, about 10 to 15 minutes.

Spread @frozen-broccoli-florets{1%package} straight from the freezer over the mesh basket of the #crisper-tray in a single layer, with space between the florets; don't thaw them. Break up any clumps. The mesh lets the melting ice drip away instead of steaming the broccoli.

Roast on the middle rack for ~dry-roast{12%minute}, until the ice has cooked off and the florets look dry.

Drizzle @avocado-oil{2%tsp} over the florets and sprinkle with @garlic-powder{1/2%tsp}, @kosher-salt{1/4%tsp}, and @black-pepper{1/4%tsp}. Toss right on the tray with tongs, spread them out again, and roast for ~roast{10%minute} more, until the edges are browned and a little charred. Oil goes on only now: on frozen florets it traps the water and they steam instead of brown.

Divide between 2 meal prep containers (about 200 g each) and let cool before sealing. Reheat in the #microwave for about a minute.
